We also went across Normalisation where we saw the 5 levels of Normalisation. 

In first normalisation the table maintains the atomicity of table data wehre. 
So as we go higher in levels of normalisation say like N1, N2, N3, etc. then we closer to the granularity of fields in the tbale and we try to get them separated or inndividual row level entries. 
Basically it is a process of breaking down fields into their granular form. 

So he explained that when we are working in industry then client will have requirements like we will be building a powerbi dashboard to bring all the unique records which is an expensive computation cost for the company so that where the normalisation concepts comes into picture and it will reduce the time of running a querry on raw table which takes 2 hpurs to come down to say like 2 seconds when the data normalised. 

So for cost efficiency we have to use normalization and for machine learning we use denormalisation. 

So in MySQL there is no syntax to join the tables with Fulll Outer Join so we use UNION of left join and right join.

In SQL your answer will be hidden in the question istelf. We just have to breakdown the question and focus on what is asked. 
We also saw the WHERE EXISTS keyword which is acting like a INNER JOIN inside a sub query.

